h96-desktop (8.0.0~r19) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Upgrade restarts running h96-power-profiles daemon (try-restart): new
    profile code applied without reboot (earlier upgrades left old daemon
    running until reboot).
  * h96-display status 'wire:' range is quantization range sent to display
    (HDMI controller status; VOP2 field only when status has none). When
    kernel EDID lists no RGB range select, line notes that 6.12 driver
    sends display default and range setting is not applied.
  * h96-vrr: HDMI variable refresh switch, off by default, experimental
    (blanking seen on some displays). 'on' runs display detect with VRR
    first and changes switch files only after detect succeeds; Xorg
    VariableRefresh snippet in /usr/share/h96/xorg.
  * edid_merge.py keeps display FreeSync range block and HDMI 2.1 VRR
    range in kernel EDID while /etc/h96/display-vrr.on exists (h96-vrr
    on); off: bytes as before.

