h96-desktop (8.0.0~r16) resolute; urgency=medium

  * h96-display, h96-display-wake.sh and h96-scdc use display of active
    session (Xorg on :1 after Wayland session in same boot broke them);
    behaviour on :0 unchanged.
  * h96-scale in Plasma Wayland session sets output scale through
    kscreen-doctor and reads it back; exits 1 when scale did not change
    (wrote X11 settings only and reported success).
  * h96-scdc set-mode passes Wayland socket to kscreen-doctor, skips
    xrandr fallback on Wayland and prints reason on failure, so
    h96-display revert no longer exits 1 without message.
  * Power-saver profile: schedutil on all clusters, CPU floor 408 MHz, big
    cores capped at 1800 MHz, little cores at 1416 MHz (was powersave
    governor pinned at 408 MHz, which dropped frames at 4K60); GPU range
    and deep idle unchanged.
  * DDR frequency scaling (6.12 kernel, dmc devfreq): performance profile
    pins DDR floor at its top rate, balanced and power-saver restore
    lowest rate; skipped where kernel has no dmc node.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000

